<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent terminal suspends berthings.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent terminal suspends berthings.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berthing was suspended at the Sullom Voe Brent Blend crude oil terminal on the Shetland islands early on Sunday because of high winds which were expected to continue into Tuesday, a port official said on Monday.</p>
<p>He said berthing was suspended at 0700 GMT on Sunday. Two tanker loadings scheduled for Monday will be postponed.</p>
<p>Gusty west to northwest winds of 15-30 miles per hour  were expected to persist in the North Sea on Monday, said independent forecaster Weather Services Corp.</p>
<p>Moderate to strong winds were also expected on Tuesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
